{
    "background_story": "Liberty was a majestic buffalofish who ruled the depths of the Mississippi River. Her scales glistened like polished copper, and her fins rippled with a quiet strength. For years, Liberty had been the guardian of the river's hidden treasures, a keeper of secrets and a whisperer of ancient tales. Fish from far and wide would gather around her to hear stories of the river's history and magic. Liberty's wisdom and kindness earned her the respect of all who lived in the river's ecosystem. One fateful day, a group of young fish got trapped in a sunken net. Liberty used her powerful tail to break free the net, freeing the trapped fish. From that day on, she was hailed as a hero and a symbol of freedom, her name Liberty becoming synonymous with bravery and selflessness.",
